# Web-dev workbench: the one private key file (EXAMPLE; it holds no real keys and never should)
#
# Your real file lives at:   ~/.config/webtools/keys.env
# Every workbench tool that needs a key reads this one file: the web tools (cf-api, wrangler-safe, bearer-curl,
# forms-check, builds_watch.py, preview_url_watch.py) and the helper with_keys.py.
# Make it like this, in YOUR OWN terminal (not in a chat with an AI):
#
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/webtools && chmod 700 ~/.config/webtools
#   [ -f ~/.config/webtools/keys.env ] || cp keys.env.example ~/.config/webtools/keys.env
#   chmod 600 ~/.config/webtools/keys.env        # only you can read it
#   # then add each key with the hidden-input command in SERVICES.md, Section A, Step 5
#
# Rules (the tools enforce them):
#   - One KEY=value per line. No spaces around "=". No quotes, no "export".
#   - Lines starting with "#" are ignored.
#   - A key you do not use stays EMPTY (nothing after "="). The tools treat an empty key as missing, and the
#     workbench uses the MANUAL route for that service.
#   - It must be a regular file you own (not a link), mode 600: the tools refuse anything else.
#   - Never copy this file into a project folder, a git repository, a cloud drive, an email or a chat.
#   - Never paste a key into a conversation with Claude or any AI assistant. You type it here yourself.
#   - Check the permissions any time:  ls -l ~/.config/webtools/keys.env   ->  must start with -rw-------
#   - Nothing should ever `source` this file. Give a command a key only through the tools or with_keys.py:
#       python3 ~/.config/webtools/with_keys.py --check CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN
#       python3 ~/.config/webtools/with_keys.py CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN,CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID -- npx wrangler@4 whoami

# --- Cloudflare (SERVICES.md, Section D; DEPLOY_CLOUDFLARE.md) -------------------------------------
# A custom API token scoped to one account (and one zone only if needed), with an expiry.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
# Not secrets, but they belong here rather than in chat. The zone ID is optional (cf-api paths with {zone}).
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID=

# --- Cloudflare Access service token, optional (SERVICES.md, Section F) ----------------------------
# Only for command-line checks of protected previews (preview_url_watch.py). Browser login needs neither line.
CF_ACCESS_CLIENT_ID=
CF_ACCESS_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Vercel (SERVICES.md, Section E; DEPLOY_VERCEL.md) ---------------------------------------------
# A token scoped to one team, with an expiration.
VERCEL_TOKEN=
# Optional: the Protection Bypass for Automation secret, for command-line checks of protected previews.
VERCEL_AUTOMATION_BYPASS_SECRET=

# --- Google Gemini API, image drafts (SERVICES.md, Section B) --------------------------------------
# A key in a Google Cloud project used only for this, restricted to the Generative Language API.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# --- Sanity, optional, for resource hubs (SERVICES.md, Section G) ----------------------------------
# A project API token with the narrowest role the work needs (read-only "Viewer" for checks).
SANITY_API_TOKEN=

# --- Deploy hook, optional (SERVICES.md, Section H) ------------------------------------------------
# A Workers Builds or Vercel deploy hook URL. The URL itself is the secret: anyone holding it can trigger a build.
DEPLOY_HOOK_URL=

# --- NOT in this file -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Flow (video passages) has no key here: it is always the manual route, in your browser.
# GitHub sign-in lives in your SSH key (~/.ssh) or the gh tool's own login, never here.
# Settings that are not secrets (folders, model names) do not belong here.
